  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for Human Biology (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 14+17+17+14+14+16+14+14 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Science (standard for AIC biology programs; the plan does not print a degree abbreviation). MAT1840 College Algebra and Trigonometry is 4 credits; MAT2400 Calculus I is 4 credits; MAT2004 Biostatistics is 3 credits (Gen Ed Category 1). Lab courses are 4 credits and include the lab section (e.g., BIO1200 lecture + BIO1201 lab = 4 credits total). Junior Fall: choose BIO2400 Comparative Vertebrate Anatomy with lab OR BIO2410 Animal Histology with lab. Sophomore Spring: BIO2200 Pathophysiology or a general elective; Junior Spring: an elective or BIO2200 Pathophysiology (BIO2200 is taken once). 'BIO3XXX Biology elective, or CHE3200 Introduction to Biochemistry with lab (CHE3201)' slots are 4-credit upper-level biology/biochemistry electives (majors need a minimum of 8 semester hours of elective credits from the approved list). Senior research/internship slots: choose BIO4833 Research Problems or BIO4899 Biology Internship (or an elective for the Senior Fall slot). The plan notes MAT1630 College Algebra is recommended for students needing math support, pushing MAT1840/MAT2400 to Year 2 (MAT1630 counts as a general elective). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
